  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Chloroform (b.p 334 K) and aniline (b.p. 457 K) are easily separated by the technique of distillation.</p><p>One of the technological applications of fractional distillation is to separate different fractions of crude oil in the petroleum industry.</p><p>Aniline is separated by steam distillation technique from aniline &ndash; water mixture.</p><p>When an organic compound is present in an aqueous medium, it is separated by shaking&nbsp;it with an organic solvent in which it is more soluble than in water.</p><p>Hence, correct matching is given by the below table:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 350px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">List I (Mixture)</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">List II<br />\t\t\t(Separation<br />\t\t\tTechnique)</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Distillation</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>14</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Fractional<br />\t\t\tdistillation</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Steam distillation</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Organic compound in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Differential<br />\t\t\textraction</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>",
